# TeleLink agent operations

When the user asks to send a message, read messages, check notifications, missed calls, or any TeleLink task:

1. **Read `AGENTS.md`** at repo root (or run `.\telelink.ps1 agent context` for live JSON).
2. **Run `.\telelink.ps1 <command>`** — do not search the codebase first.

## Quick commands

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| **What did X send me?** | `.\telelink.ps1 received mom` |
| Read SMS thread (both ways) | `.\telelink.ps1 convo "Name" --raw` |
| Read notifications | `.\telelink.ps1 caught --raw --limit 10` |
| Send SMS | `.\telelink.ps1 send "Name" message` |
| Schedule SMS | `.\telelink.ps1 send in%2hour% "Name" message` |
| Last attachment | `data/.analyze/latest.json` + `latest.png` |
| Contacts | `.\telelink.ps1 contacts` |

Draft SMS using `owner.talking_tone` from `agent context` — never paste `@tone` into the message body.

`received` = incoming SMS only (full text, JSON). `convo` = full thread. `caught` = notification toasts.
